# Decisions Log

- 2026-07-21: Chosen genre is mind-bending sci-fi with modern prose and poetic inflection.
- 2026-07-21: Target length is ~10,000 words to keep the experiment manageable.
- 2026-07-21: Project structure follows software development phases and supports branching experiments.
- 2026-07-21: Added a subtle antagonist named The Limit, which begins as a peripheral presence and becomes a direct philosophical opposite to Keji's final choice.
- 2026-07-21: Created a more detailed story outline and a philosophy guide to anchor the writing process.
- 2026-08-21: Adopted an executable test suite: mechanically checkable prose rules moved to `tests/automated/rules.yaml`, enforced by `tools/check_story.py`; judgment checklists moved to `tests/manual/`. New violations must be added to `rules.yaml` (regression protocol).
- 2026-08-21: Replaced the monolithic validation report with a generated `tests/STATUS.md` plus a living manual-review record in `tests/VALIDATION_REPORT.md`.
- 2026-08-21: Added `src/01-world/canon.md` as the continuity ledger; `tests/manual/consistency.md` now checks drafts against it.
- 2026-08-21: Added `tools/build_manuscript.py` and an ordered chapter list in `book.yaml`; `chapter_final_speculative.md` excluded from the default build pending the ch11/speculative ending decision.
- 2026-08-21: Automation flagged open issues: duplicate titles (ch3/ch7 "The Limit", ch4/ch10 "The Erased Core") and "had learned" in the speculative ending. Left for story revision, not fixed by tooling.
- 2026-08-21: Iteration pass 1 (story): retitled ch7 "The Table of Light" and ch10 "The Yes and the No"; removed ~20 authorial framing constructions ("not X. It was Y.", significance summaries, narrator explanations of theme) from ch2-ch11; varied repeated body-sensation verbs; trimmed pocket/word-phrase hotspots. Word count 10,453 -> 9,664 (authorial fat removed).
- 2026-08-21: Chapter 11 declared the canonical ending; speculative ending archived to drafts/chapter_final_speculative.md (not canon, excluded from build).
- 2026-08-21: Editing convention adopted (docs/style_guide.md, Language): a word mentioned as a word must stay marked ("the word X" framing or quotes); bare placement after speech verbs or as sentence subject is ambiguous and prohibited.
- 2026-08-21: Frequency caps tuned against counts: "the word" max_total raised 15 -> 20 (deliberate device of the story; per-chapter cap of 3 is the drift guard).
- 2026-08-21: Manual validation of chapters 2-11 completed and recorded in tests/VALIDATION_REPORT.md. Automated suite: 0 errors, 0 warnings across 11 chapters. Known polish candidate: ch11's closing movement is dry (no tidal echo); see motif_usage.md.
- 2026-08-21: Word-count policy changed: 10k is a floor, not a target; hard ceiling 20k. Any cutting pass happens only at final polish, if needed.
- 2026-08-21: Added measurement suite: scene/ambiguity/relationship/promise ledgers in tests/analysis/ validated by the checker, plus tools/analyze_story.py (frequency, trigrams, rhythm, dialogue, voice fingerprints, emotion lexicons). Baseline quantified 18 structural failures matching the 5.2/10 assessment.
- 2026-08-21: Revision pass 2 driven by ledgers: lived memories for Lio (ch1 tidepool, ch2 coins) and Ira (ch5 kitchen); mercy evidence for the central ambiguity (ch4 earlier take, ch5 lighthouse sketch); real costs extracted (ch9 crushed fingers, ch10 permanent seal, ch11 Ari's seals); civic stakes via Drift burst (ch10); warmth restored to finale (quay beat). Re-scored 5.2 -> 6.9; see docs/story_assessment_2026-08-21.md revision 2 section.
- 2026-08-21: Remaining known weaknesses after revision 2: dialogue voice distinctness (~5), image density ("wall" ~94/10k), Keji's final choice still personally cheap, want-vs-need never forced.
- 2026-08-21: Added reading-experience suite (criteria 41-50 in the rubric): tension curve, open-loops, plant/payoff, attachment, world-term onboarding, surprise profile, and reception ledgers, all validated by the checker. Suite immediately caught: 'a film of film' typo (ch4, fixed), 'node' drifting 4 chapters without grounding (fixed via ch6 dialogue beat), 3 open plants (whistle, maintenance key, Ari's phrase — documented work items). Reader-experience supplement scored 6.5/10; combined overall 6.8.
- 2026-08-21: Revision pass 4 executed the reading-experience punch list: whistle/key/phrase plants paid (ch11 quay, ch10 seam, ch11 exit); false-calm valley added (ch8, tension 2); act-3 want stated at ch9 close; council price delayed past one breath of relief (ch11). New crystallized tests: TN-06/07 peak-valley counts, SL-07 final-choice dilemma gate, analyzer sentence-opener + abstract-agent + dialogue-music metrics. Line pass thinned Keji/wall density in ch6-ch7. Combined score 6.8 -> 7.1; remaining sub-7 criteria are promise, escalation, midpoint, reveal timing, image economy, genre contract, voices — next lifts need new scenes or reference-corpus calibration, not edits alone.
- 2026-08-21: Added coupling layer: metric interaction map (docs/metric_interactions.md), pillar report with spread penalties (tools/pillar_report.py -> tests/PILLARS.md; raw 7.10 vs system-adjusted 6.76), machine-readable scores (scores_current.yaml) + history snapshots, staleness report in analyzer (chapter similarity, words-per-info, flat chapters), and tension x emotional-breadth coupling. Actions taken from first runs: ch6 compressed (removals archived to drafts/scene_archive_2026-08-21.md — new convention: nothing silently deleted), ch9 narrow peak fixed with a gentle beat inside the spike (tension-emotion correlation -0.04 -> +0.26). Structure Spine identified as the pillar stuck since r2 — the next pass's primary target.
- 2026-08-21: Revision pass 5 (Structure Spine): failed public attempt with surveillance seed (ch8), annotation-refusal before the injury cost (ch9), and the ribbon reveal — the glitch is Ira's own smuggled recording, cut clean mid-sentence (ch10), paying the story's oldest plant and recutting ch1/ch5. Suite caught the loop-budget consequence live: RQ6 closed (answered by enforcement behavior), RQ2/RQ4 merged into one reader question-cluster. Structure Spine 6.15 -> 7.15; raw overall 7.10 -> 7.20; system-adjusted 6.76 -> 6.88. No pillar below 6 for the first time; weakest remaining: Promise Frame (promise #2, genre #40).
- 2026-08-21: Reference-corpus calibration: four PD works fetched and cleaned into references/ (Machine Stops, Metamorphosis, Yellow Wallpaper, Mrs Dalloway in Bond Street); analyzer run over them -> docs/reference_calibration.md. Evidence: our opener dominance and abstract-agent density are real mannerisms vs canon (~0); sentence-variance low (stdev 5.8 vs 12-17 band) recorded as aspiration; em-dash usage normal; awe/wonder starved (1.0 vs 5.3/10k). Opener flag tightened 25% -> 15%.
- 2026-08-21: Promise Frame work: book titled "Something Was Left Behind" (was "Untitled"); ch1 gains a city-scale promise line ("the Archive did not glitch for one person"); P1 red-team finding fixed same-session ("The city is a palimpsest" label removed); Sera reliability question added at quay (ch11) — "When did you last read your own archive?" — opening held-deliberate loop RQ8 and ambiguity q4 (memories authentic vs edited).
- 2026-08-21: Red-team protocol built (tests/redteam/personas.md) and first run recorded (REDTEAM_REPORT_2026-08-21.md). Success test partially met: three scenes praised unprompted by >=2 personas (ribbon reveal, ch9 injury, quay sequence). Scores adopted: #2 -> 7, #40 -> 7. Raw overall 7.24; system-adjusted 6.96.
- 2026-08-21: Red-team round 2 with four new personas (line editor, continuity auditor, impatient skimmer, representation reader) appended to the report. Triage same-session: glitch-retrieval gap fixed (ch3), coin re-pocket shown (ch11), three abstract-agents converted, ch7 opening compressed, awe beat seeded in ch10 burst aftermath; institution/care gendering recorded as intentional pattern in canon watchlist; Ira/Lio pronoun-neutrality verified and watchlist item closed. Banked: ch6 first-third compression (next pass target); "The"-opener share 28% vs canon ~8% is the largest remaining quantified mannerism. No criterion score changes this round.
